# SailGuard

On-prem endpoint application control. Module path: `github.com/ekkywi/sailguard`.

## Collaboration

- User often codes manually: give small steps and explain purpose; do not dump full implementations unless asked.
- Never silently remove planned features from checklists to “simplify” for solo pace.
- Pace is flexible; order follows `docs/internal/roadmap.md` / checklist.

## Docs

- `docs/public/` — shareable product documentation (no lab passwords, no security-gap lists). **Committed.**
- `docs/internal/` — engineering truth (checklist, merge, API matrix, handoff). **Gitignored — local only.**
- Continuity: keep `docs/internal/handoff.md` + `CONTINUE_PROMPT.md` on each machine you use (copy privately).
- Academic path: `docs/internal/academic-path.md` (magang prototipe → skripsi pengembangan). Do not inflate internship scope into full thesis work without the user asking.

## Runtime (dev)

- Compose: Postgres + Redis only.
- Host: API `127.0.0.1:18080`, Web `127.0.0.1:15180`, Postgres `15433`, Redis `16380`.
- See `docs/internal/ports.md`.

## Data changes

- Schema + RBAC catalog → goose migrations.
- Lab admin users → `seeds/development/`.
- Prefer `make migrate-up` (goose may live in `$(go env GOPATH)/bin`).
